A||||5||My7Fieros||Need help with distributor? (HEI).....Kinda need some help fast please!!!||||11||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||01-12-2001||10:53 AM||||I get in the 86 SE (V6, the one in my sig pic), and when I started it the check engine light came on. I pulled the codes and got a code 42..Electronic Spark Timing.<BR>Upon reading the Haynes manual, it states that "a malfunctioning HEI module can cause this trouble code". Upon reading what exactly the HEI is (High Energy Ignition), Im gathering that what its getting at is that either the pick up coil or the ignition control module may be going bad.....is this the case, and if so, which one? <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||11
Z||000001||Songman||01-12-2001||11:25 AM||||It is a total guess but I am going to say module. I don't think the coil will throw any codes in the computer. <P>From what I have seen in my past with working on cars, the coil may cause erratic idle and stuff like that while it is going out and then eventually just die. But I really don't think it causes codes. This is all a guess because I have never worked on HEI in a Fiero. I don't know if it works like HEI in V8 cars.<P>Have there been any other symptoms other than the check engine light? If not, reset the computer and see if it throws codes again.<P>---------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://homepages.go.com/homepages/t/n/f/tnfieros/TNFiero.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 01-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||01-12-2001||11:45 AM||||It's the module. I had the same thing on my car a while back. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||01-12-2001||12:46 PM||||Does the car show any symptoms?  FWIW, my 1986 V6 SE 4-speed wouldn't start after it was parked for a week or so in an airport parking lt - cranked and cranked - no start. Opened hood to look at engine - saw nothing obvious - shut hood. Got back in car, and it started immediately.<P>At home, read out trouble codes - it showed code 42.  Cleared codes; did nothing else to the car.  Still starts and runs fine 12 years  later - original coil, pickup coil & module.<P>My point?  Maybe it's nothing.  Wouldn't blame you if you bought a decent replacement   module to carry with you just in case, though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">!  Just one Fiero owner's experience. ||||reg||5
Z||000004||My7Fieros||01-12-2001||01:06 PM||||Ok thats what I thought to...module..kinda suspected that since Ive never noticed the pick up throwing a code before like Songman said. Anywho I went on and replaced the ignition controle module and she runs fine again. Thanx all!!!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000005||Fiero Fanatic||01-12-2001||05:15 PM||||After reading all the posts on modules. I went to a wrecking yard and gathered about 3 of them. They all tested good. Now I'm waiting for my first one to go bad  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. Knock on wood!!!||||reg||1
